These values keep the correct sign feedback (negative on position/velocity, positive on angle/angular‑velocity) while reducing the dominant ω‑term that caused frequent saturation in the best‑so‑far policy. By scaling down the angular‑velocity weight from 2.5 to 1.5 and modestly increasing the angle gain, the controller can generate sufficient corrective force without hitting the ±3 N limit, lowering drift and sign‑flipping. The position weight is strengthened to -5.0 to pull the cart back toward centre, and a small bias is omitted to let the state‑feedback dominate. This balanced, lower‑gain linear policy is expected to extend episode length beyond the current 49.6 benchmark.
