response-og: params[0]: -1.0, params[1]: 6.0, params[2]: -0.5, params[3]: 2.5, params[4]: 0.0  
I chose a negative weight for cart position (-1.0) to generate a corrective force opposite to any positional drift, while keeping a strong positive gain on pole angle (6.0) to apply the appropriate directional push when the pole leans. The moderate negative velocity gain (-0.5) helps damp cart speed, and the positive angular‑velocity gain (2.5) adds damping to pole motion. A zero bias avoids systematic offset, aiming to keep the system centered longer and increase episode length.
